<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 1">
  <data key="d2">Step 1: Wash the rice well and so...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Wash the rice well and soak it for 20 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d4">1</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 2">
  <data key="d2">Step 2: Drain completely.</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Drain completely.</data>
  <data key="d4">2</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 3">
  <data key="d2">Step 3: Heat coconut oil in a hea...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Heat coconut oil in a heavy-bottomed pot.</data>
  <data key="d4">3</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 4">
  <data key="d2">Step 4: Add the bay leaf, cinnamo...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Add the bay leaf, cinnamon stick, cardamoms, and cloves.</data>
  <data key="d4">4</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 5">
  <data key="d2">Step 5: Sauté for 20-30 seconds u...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Sauté for 20-30 seconds until fragrant.</data>
  <data key="d4">5</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 6">
  <data key="d2">Step 6: Add the drained rice and ...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Add the drained rice and gently sauté for 1 minute.</data>
  <data key="d4">6</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 7">
  <data key="d2">Step 7: Pour in the coconut milk ...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Pour in the coconut milk and water.</data>
  <data key="d4">7</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 8">
  <data key="d2">Step 8: Add the salt and sugar, t...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Add the salt and sugar, then mix gently.</data>
  <data key="d4">8</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 9">
  <data key="d2">Step 9: Bring it to a gentle boil...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Bring it to a gentle boil, cover with a tight-fitting lid and cook on the lowest heat for 12-15 minutes.</data>
  <data key="d4">9</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 10">
  <data key="d2">Step 10: Once the rice is cooked, ...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Once the rice is cooked, switch off the flame. At this stage, the rice may look slightly soft because the trapped steam is still carrying moisture.</data>
  <data key="d4">10</data>
</node>
<node id="[Coconut Rice] Step 11">
  <data key="d2">Step 11: Let it rest, covered, for...</data>
  <data key="d0">Step</data>
  <data key="d1">#F1C40F</data>
  <data key="d3">Let it rest, covered, for 10 minutes. During this time, the steam redistributes evenly through the rice and the starch begins to set, making the grains light, fluffy and well-separated.</data>
  <data key="d4">11</data>
</node>
